      players: '2 to 4 players. Can be played in partnerships (2 vs 2).',
      deck: 'Standard double-six set (28 tiles).',
      equipment: 'Domino set, flat surface.',
      dealing: "Tiles are shuffled face-down ('washing'). Players draw a hand (usually 7 tiles for 2 players, 5 for 3-4 players). Remaining tiles form the 'boneyard'.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Starting: The player with the highest double leads (usually the 6-6).\n2. Matching: Players take turns placing a tile so that one end matches an open end of the line of play.\n3. Drawing: In 'Draw' dominoes, if you cannot move, you must draw from the boneyard until a move is possible. In 'Block' dominoes, you simply pass.\n4. Blocking: If no player can move and the boneyard is empty, the game is blocked.",
